WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.195
Although designed for federal environments,

00:00:02.195 --> 00:00:05.840
NIST SP 800-53 is frequently used outside government.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.090
Many organizations use the catalog as a reference for building mature security and privacy

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:10.660
programs.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.920
Organizations often map controls to internal policies, customer requirements,

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.136
regulatory obligations, and other frameworks.

00:00:17.136 --> 00:00:20.990
This mapping helps teams translate broad security goals into specific control

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:21.960
expectations.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.985
Commercial adoption happens because the catalog is comprehensive and well understood.

00:00:25.985 --> 00:00:29.825
It gives organizations a common way to discuss safeguards even when formal federal

00:00:29.825 --> 00:00:31.230
compliance is not required.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.240
Using the catalog outside government still requires judgment.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.030
Teams should adapt the controls to their mission, systems, resources, laws,

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.280
and risk environment.
